# Milestone: M3
# Covers: atomicity of single-cycle operations under the urbiscript scheduler;
#         'atomic' pattern using call.evalArgAt(0) and System.cycle comparison.
# defer-to: M5 (requires System.cycle, call.evalArgAt, Semaphore, and '&'/'|' runtime)
#
# Reason:
#   This fixture uses call.evalArgAt(0) for lazy parameter evaluation (M4
#   object/reflection model), System.cycle counter (M4 stdlib), Semaphore type
#   (M6 stdlib), and nested '&' separator (M5 chk driver).  None of these are
#   available in the M3 uvm_run REPL path.
#
# Original urbiscript (activate at M5+ with full stdlib):
# # function atomic { var start = System.cycle | call.evalArgAt(0) | assert(System.cycle == start) }|;
# # atomic(1+2);
# # atomic({var n = 0});
# # ... (see legacy/repos/aldebaran-urbi/tests/2.x/atomic.chk)
